      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "For $\\frac{9}{4}$, we can simply find the ceiling of $\\frac{9}{4}$, which is $\\boxed{3}$, and the ceiling of $\\frac{9}{2}$, which is $\\boxed{5}$.\nTo evaluate the given expression, we will calculate each term separately:\n\n1.  $\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} \\approx sqrt(2.25)=2.24$\nwhich is equal to $2$\n\n2. $\\frac{9}{4} = 2.25$, which is equal to $2$.\n\n3. $\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{81}{16} = 5.0625$ which is equal to $5$\n\nSo, the expression becomes $\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 2 + 5 = \\boxed{9}$.",
